// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 12-type-system
// facility: rule.fn.generic-call [Generic-Call-Uninferable]; rule.agg.array-construct; conf.empty-array-literal-uninferable
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.cannot-infer-type-parameter (static)
//
// An empty array literal is typed by its declaration ([Array-Construct]
// with N = 0); with `auto` nothing fixes its element type, so the
// binding is refused as `auto v = Vec::new();` is. Until Update 213 the
// checker gave it a placeholder `array<i32, 0>` and the compiler faulted
// while lowering the program.

import std;

fn main()
{
    auto x = [];
    printf("%d\n", 1);
}
